        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "05c41e7b-0c25-5819-9917-2e972e043781",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: English National Ballet, English National Opera, BBC Television\n- Places: London Coliseum, Royal Albert Hall, St. Martin's Lane, central London\n- People: Alina Cojocaru, Frank Matcham, Oswald Stoll\n- Works: Doctor Ox's Experiment\n\nFacts:\n- The London Coliseum opened on 24 December 1904 in St. Martin's Lane, central London, as the London Coliseum Theatre of Varieties.\n- The London Coliseum was designed by Frank Matcham for Oswald Stoll as one of London's largest and most luxurious family variety theatres.\n- Doctor Ox's Experiment was first performed on 15 June 1998 at the London Coliseum by English National Opera, which co-commissioned the opera with BBC Television.\n- As of November 2013, Alina Cojocaru was a principal dancer with the English National Ballet.\n- The English National Ballet regularly performs seasons at the London Coliseum.\n- The English National Ballet has also been noted for specially staged performances at the Royal Albert Hall.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
